{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Sharpened the consequence the reopened snapshot question now turns on. The earlier wording had a recovered save panic leaving the apply loop skipping the cluster; reading the status checks shows that holds only for a state machine without concurrent snapshot support, where a missing save completion makes processSaveStatus report the cluster busy on every pass. With concurrent snapshotting the apply loop continues, and the residue is that every later save is refused while the stuck flag is set, so the snapshot duty is lost without a node-wide stall. The busy-snapshotting predicate also turns out not to rescue either case, since it requires a busy task channel that a dead worker leaves empty, so a new save would be requested and then refused rather than the flag clearing. The gap answer, counterevidence and limitations now carry that distinction, and the question stays conditional on the dependency's launcher.\"}"}}
